From: gbagate
Subject: [PATCH] Ack timeout follows the line; resends wait twice as long each

Base: Celio-Link/Celio-Server 8f509bd.

emitWithRetry waited a fixed 1 s for each ack, 5 times, 100 ms apart, then
ended the session. On a line with a round trip near or over 1 s every copy
timed out before its ack could arrive, and socket.io drops an ack that comes
after its timeout, so even the first copy's late ack was thrown away.

- Each copy waits twice as long as the last (1, 2, 4, 8, 8, 8 s), as TCP
  backs off its retransmit timer.
- Every copy listens for its ack until the last copy's time is up, so a late
  ack for an earlier copy counts.
- The first wait is twice the smoothed round trip once one is known (7/8 old,
  1/8 new, first sends only: Karn's rule), never under 1 s or over 8 s.
- pingTimeout 2000 -> 5000: Engine.IO dropped the socket of any client whose
  round trip neared 2 s.

Measured with gbagate's test/gblink_compat/test_celio_latency.mjs (two
clients, delay and jitter on each client's socket): see backport/README.md.

